# Git hooks are run by sh, and sh does not strip \r. With core.autocrlf=true
# (the default on this machine) a checkout would rewrite them CRLF, and
# `|| true` becomes `|| true\r`: command not found. The failure is silent in
# a post-* hook and blocks every commit in pre-commit. Measured as a warning
# at `git add` on 12 September 2026, the day core.hooksPath began pointing at
# the tracked copies -- the .git/hooks copy had never been through checkout.
tools/hooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh           text eol=lf
